# Monitor: BeeGFS client (`beegfs_client`)

## Detection

- Enumerate mounts with fstype **`beegfs`** or **`beegfs_nodev`** (`/proc/mounts`).
- Device id is the **mount path** (e.g. `/scratch`).
- `/proc/fs/beegfs/<clientID>/` on BeeGFS **7.3.x** exposes config/state only — **no** cumulative I/O counter files (`ops-rd` / `MiB-rd` absent). Do not invent procfs counter parsers for 7.3.x.

## Capacity (cheap, every sample)

- `statvfs(3)` on the mount → `fs_bytes_*` / `fs_files_*` (same semantics as `lustre_llite`).

## I/O and metadata (bounded `beegfs-ctl`)

- On 7.3.x there is **no public linkable clientstats library**; use **`beegfs-ctl --clientstats`**.
- **Equals-form argv only (7.3.4+):** `--nodetype=storage|meta`, `--cfgFile=<path>`, `--interval=0`, `--perinterval`, `--names`, optional `--rwunit=B`. **Never** two-token `--nodetype storage` or `--mount /path` — on 7.3.4 the bare token is a `<nodeID>` / invalid mount and ctl fails (`Invalid NodeNumID` / `Given mountpoint is invalid`).
- Prefer **`--cfgFile=`** from mount `cfgFile=` (fallback `/etc/beegfs/beegfs-client.conf`). Do not rely on two-token `--mount` for `beegfs_nodev`.
- Prefer **`--rwunit=B`** when supported (`B-rd` / `B-wr`); else parse `MiB-rd` / `MiB-wr` (scientific notation OK) and scale **× 1048576** to `vfs_read_bytes` / `vfs_write_bytes`.
- Map ctl abbreviations to portable **`vfs_*`** keys (see `beegfs_client.h`); never emit raw `MiB-rd` / `ops-rd` / `unlnk` as KEY names.
- **Never** ingest the cluster **`Sum:`** line as this host’s counters — select the **local** line via hostname / short hostname / **`hostname-ib`** / local IPv4 (`--names` often prints InfiniBand hostnames).
- Keep wall-time budget on ctl (timeout → skip; first-fail log; capacity still works).
- **Jitter:** when `enable_slow_tier` is on, refresh ctl only on **`COLLECT_FULL`**; when off, at most once per `max(sample_freq, 30s)`. Emit ctl-derived keys only on refresh ticks (tier table marks `vfs_*` slow; `fs_*` stay fast).
- **dmesg `beegfs: enabling unsafe global rkey`:** kernel log on **new RDMA protection domain** create (ThinkParQ FAQ). Working equals-form `clientstats` does not by itself reproduce a per-sample storm; do not “fix” it by rewriting site `beegfs-client.conf` / `connRDMAKeyType` from the monitor.

## Configure

- **`--enable-beegfs`** default **yes**; `MONITOR_WITH_BEEGFS`; capability slug fragment **`beegfs`**.
- Missing `beegfs-ctl` with mounts present: detect + capacity still work; **no** per-sample ERROR spam.

## Tests

- Schema contract rejects raw ctl names; ctl parse fixtures cover Sum ignore, MiB→bytes, hostname match.
- Argv builder tests assert equals-form tokens and absence of two-token `--nodetype` / `--mount`.
- Ident helper tests assert `short-ib` / `fqdn-ib` aliases (not for IPv4).

